From 5523579bb5afe70a4341174c1614a99ba2f150ce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 04:17:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/8] fix(gateway): keep caller credentials away from inference
 instances

The stream proxy copied every inbound header to the selected inference
instance, including Authorization and Cookie. With API key
authentication those headers carry the caller's platform credential, and
an instance (which may run third-party model server code) could replay it
against the control plane as that tenant.

Drop Authorization and Cookie when forwarding to instances. The resolver
still sends the caller's Authorization to the control plane, which needs
it to verify the caller.
---
 gateway/internal/router/auth_test.go  | 23 +++++++++++++++--------
 gateway/internal/stream/proxy.go      | 15 +++++++++++++--
 gateway/internal/stream/proxy_test.go | 16 +++++++++-------
 3 files changed, 37 insertions(+), 17 deletions(-)

